  "notes": "The issue fixed workers sending keys their candidate tools refuse, and measured the fix with a code-scored evaluation. It grew the most of these five: 327 words at first, 1,035 when the first PR (#284) opened on 2026-11-09, and 2,740 at the end, over 18 versions. Most growth came on 2026-11-09 after #284 opened, as Joe settled questions in chat and the Do list took on new steps, decisions and results. By the end the Do section mixes all three. Three Do items are pure results (I266-29, I266-30, I266-33), and a struck Do item holds the decision to leave the rating key alone (I266-31). Two open questions were never struck, even though the work answered them (I266-10, I266-15). Results show up in all three places: the body's Do, issue comments (the corpus count IC266-4, the baseline IC266-6, and run counts in IC266-0 to IC266-3), and the PR descriptions (P285-d8 to d13, P286-d6 to d13). Most struck question answers are task (I266-12, I266-14, I266-16, I266-17), but some just say see Do (I266-11, I266-18). The PR descriptions copy Do items (P285-d2 to d7), but #284's also adds new material: Joe's request from chat (P284-d1), a log of test steps (P284-d13 to d17), and setup steps for running the evaluation (P284-d18 to d29). Across the three decisions comments, 5 of 14 decisions name a doc (P284-c0, P284-c1, P285-c0, P285-c1, P286-c0). One says outright that it was kept out of a doc (P284-c2). One decision that was written into a doc was later found wrong (P284-c1, fixed per I266-23)."
